      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, can u look at these traces? We're seeing some weird intermittent issues on the 10.45.0.0/24 subnet here in Lyon. Getting high jitter and some packet loss on certain hops but it's not constant. \n\nhop 1: 192.168.1.1 - 0.5ms\nhop 2: 10.0.4.1 - 12.2ms\nhop 3: 172.16.5.4 - 45.8ms (spike)\nhop 4: 172.16.5.5 - 110.2ms (spike)\nhop 5: 82.12.44.1 - 15.1ms\n\nping stats:\n2% packet loss\nloss variance (jitter) is hitting 40ms+ randomly. \nhelp me figure out if this is the local router or a physical line issue.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
